id: pm-todos-sessions
title: Reconcile todo.txt editing sessions without overwriting concurrent edits
description: "Export todo.txt with stable item and field digests; reconcile external edits against current tracker values using fidelity conversion. Overlap rechecked: pm-todos fidelity/upsert owns todo.txt conversion; pm-csv owns tables and core SDK transactions own atomicity. No existing editing-session item found; reconciliation PR 140 items excluded."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-21T20:12:43.381Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T23:15:10.292Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-24T21:48:49.643Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-22T21:59:13.000Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Concurrent local edits conflict explicitly; deleting a line never deletes an item by default; unchanged imports are idempotent; typed SDK and CLI with compact TOON/JSON and actionable refusals; non-git and public-tracker-copy validation
resolution: "Editing sessions preserve concurrent local edits as explicit conflicts, never delete items by default, and keep unchanged imports idempotent with compact actionable no-git SDK/CLI."
expected_result: Concurrent local edits conflict explicitly; deleting a line never deletes an item by default; unchanged imports are idempotent; typed SDK and CLI with compact TOON/JSON and actionable refusals; non-git and public-tracker-copy validation
actual_result: "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-todos/pull/141, merged 2026-10-22T21:59:13Z, merge e35b7f43f64ffe43c07ae26afc6744d6ae50b6d5: Editing sessions preserve concurrent local edits as explicit conflicts, never delete items by default, and keep unchanged imports idempotent with compact actionable no-git SDK/CLI."
comments[18]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T20:13:36.513Z",codex-agent,"Design: todo.txt lines carry stable pm identities; versioned sidecar carries item and field digests. Three-way field reconciliation reuses fidelity conversion; omissions retain items, unchanged imports write nothing. Final reconciliation runs inside the core SDK item lock, retaining ownership, workflow and history enforcement. Batch atomicity remains a core concern; result records per-item progress if a writer races later rows. Lifecycle changes require normal pm close/reopen and return a typed remedy. No git subprocess is required."
  "2026-10-21T20:17:57.073Z",codex-agent,"Validation: a disposable non-git copy of the public main tracker contained 92 items. Exported all 92: 10443 text bytes and 86536 sidecar bytes. Unchanged import matched 92, replay changed zero, omission retained 92, item/history/settings bytes stayed identical on no-op, concurrent title produced one field_conflict. Source fingerprints stayed unchanged. Behavioral revert: disabling only field-digest conflict detection makes the three-way regression fail (exit 1); restored implementation passes. A linked-test sandbox exposed init target precedence; the regression now supplies an explicit SDK client root."
  "2026-10-21T20:19:34.780Z",codex-agent,"Targeted validation includes simultaneous SDK writers on the same tracker (one success, one explicit conflict), installed packed CLI TOON/JSON commands, absent-git PATH, locked-item refusal, field merge, no-op durable history and omission. Typecheck and docstring lint pass; no separate lint script exists. Full npm and Bun release gates run in CI at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-21T20:21:54.154Z",codex-agent,"Pre-review hardening: digest canonicalization now uses code-unit ordering rather than locale collation, so sidecars remain stable across machines and Node versions, including Unicode metadata keys. Added insertion-order coverage. The first implementation commit is 83701c2; ready PR 141 carries CI evidence and documented per-item/lifecycle boundaries."
  "2026-10-21T20:23:53.985Z",codex-agent,"No-git regression strengthened: the isolated child now performs an actual changed-item apply with PATH containing no git executable, rather than only no-op reconciliation. Targeted real-tracker scenario passes (1/1); no product changes were needed."
  "2026-10-21T22:08:16.167Z",codex-agent,"PR #141 review round: fetched all six unresolved threads with complete comments and the latest CodeRabbit review (no additional Outside diff range findings). Verified all six findings. Plan: clean up failed exclusive exports, reject lossy title projections with item diagnostics, correct omission validation, index input lines once, strengthen invalid-calendar and mixed-batch no-write tests. Self-review the complete PR for the same defect classes. Run targeted regressions with behavioral revert proofs, typecheck and docstring gate locally; use CI npm and Bun release gates at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-21T22:10:52.114Z",codex-agent,"Implementation and self-review: exclusive export now records ownership before each write and removes owned sidecar/text outputs on open or partial-write failure; existing editing files are preserved. Title projection is checked against normalized tracker titles, including fidelity provenance, and export errors name the item. Session apply indexes full input once outside item locks while retaining duplicate validation. Validation omissions use exported entry count. Added real non-git tracker regressions for mixed known refusals (zero item/history writes), scan count, retry, partial writes and untitled validation inputs; invalid-date fixture now retains task text. Initial targeted run exposed two test assumptions: harness returns ordinary filesystem errors as handled:false receipts, and a title prefix shielded by a priority is representable. Corrected the fixtures; export-focused tests pass 3/3."
  "2026-10-21T22:12:07.799Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs (all restored afterward): PRRT_kwDOSZpews6u-EMx: restore only previous export writes; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"failed session exports|partial sidecar\" test/sessions.test.ts fails 2/2 (exit 1). PRRT_kwDOSZpews6u-EM5: restore items.length omission comparison; pattern \"validation script counts\" fails 1/1 (exit 1). PRRT_kwDOSZpews6u-ENB: restore only createTodoEditingSession; pattern \"export rejects lossy\" fails 1/1 (exit 1). PRRT_kwDOSZpews6u-ENI: restore only applyTodoEditingSession; pattern \"multi-item apply scans\" fails 1/1 (exit 1), observing 5 complete input scans for 4 patches instead of at most 2. PRRT_kwDOSZpews6u-ENO: disable only the projected calendar guard; pattern \"untrusted sessions and malformed\" fails 1/1 (exit 1), proving the corrected titled invalid-date fixture reaches calendar validation. PRRT_kwDOSZpews6u-ENX: disable only the preview refusal early return; pattern \"mixed known input refusals\" fails 1/1 (exit 1), observing applied=1 instead of 0. Each pattern command uses node --test --test-name-pattern=\"PATTERN\" test/sessions.test.ts. Tests import source, so these isolated function/guard reverts require no dist rebuild."
  "2026-10-21T22:12:40.935Z",codex-agent,"Restored implementation verification: pm test pm-todos-sessions --run --progress passed all 4 linked commands: node --test test/sessions.test.ts (10 passed, 0 failed/skipped), npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run docstring (12 files, 86 declarations). npm run build and git diff --check also passed. No local timeouts occurred. Result tracking policy keeps raw pm test receipts local, so this comment persists the public-safe summary. dist is generated and untracked in this repository. Local strict tracker health has no history drift; its only gate-failing finding is the existing pm-github host-version skew, which CI avoids by installing its pinned extension. Full release checks deferred to CI to respect shared CPU limits. No code or threshold changes outside this review scope."
  "2026-10-21T22:22:20.015Z",codex-agent,"CI verification for code commit d34fddb48582e668e614fb23e440fa9e99e78e70: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-todos/actions/runs/39684868331 completed successfully. Node 22.18.0 and 26 each passed npm run release:check AND bun run release:check. Every one of the four gates reports 316 tests passed, 0 failed/skipped; canonical-reader acceptance 1 passed; packed-host acceptance 4 scenarios passed (npm/Bun on pinned development and minimum supported hosts). Both runtime source files covered: 98.02% lines, 93.95% branches, 98.77% functions; unchanged floors 97/93/98. Tracker health, docstrings, audit, package, changelog, calendar-date and publish-attestation gates passed. No timeout retries were required. Final review fetch has the same six unresolved threads and identical complete comments; latest CodeRabbit review remains unchanged with no additional Outside diff range findings. All six valid findings and all nitpicks are addressed; no thread replies/resolutions, merge or release. Releasing the claim and leaving the item in progress for orchestrator verification; the evidence-only tracker commit will receive its own exact-head CI run."
  "2026-10-22T20:42:19.930Z",codex-agent,"PR 141 follow-up: pulled remote head 52587a6, which already includes current main. GraphQL quota exhausted; REST provided all review comments, latest CodeRabbit review (no additional Outside diff range findings), orchestrator review 5620287005 and CodeQL alert 11. Verified quadratic whitespace backtracking in session identity parsing and stale source provenance after independent field merges. Plan linear suffix parsing shared by preview and apply, fidelity serialization of the merged fields, deterministic held-lock regression, typed unreadable todo.txt errors, and explicit corruption-only sidecar digest documentation. Preserve earlier review fixes. Full isolated npm and Bun release gates and exact-head CodeQL confirmation are required."
  "2026-10-22T20:48:06.495Z",codex-agent,"Implemented linear sessionLine suffix parsing shared by plan and the apply index. Security boundary pass verified attacker-controlled CLI/SDK editing text reaches the shared parser; whitespace delimiters and anchored identity checks now have disjoint scans. Reviewed all regexes in sessions.ts and index.ts: todo.txt status/priority/date prefixes had the same whitespace/body overlap on embedded Unicode line separators, now disjoint via a non-whitespace body start. Existing markdown provenance/type suffix guards already avoid leading whitespace scans. Independent priority/tag/deadline merges now serialize source provenance from the merged structured values, preserving replay idempotency. Missing editing files raise actionable CommandError for preview/apply. Sidecar docs explicitly limit digests to corruption detection, not authenticity. Separate post-patch bypass/compatibility review traced both CLI/SDK paths, duplicate/missing delimiters, token order and current-field serialization. No delegation was used under queue rules."
  "2026-10-22T20:48:13.199Z",codex-agent,"Five isolated behavioral proofs, source imports so no dist rebuild: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"session parsing handles\" test/sessions.test.ts fails 1/1 with only sessionLine restored to the old regex (15-second child watchdog on 100k-space near misses). Pattern \"prefix parsing handles\" fails 1/1 with only parseTodoTxtLine restored (same watchdog on space runs before a Unicode line separator). Pattern \"merged source provenance\" fails 1/1 with only the old provenance block restored: stored priority C versus merged priority A. Pattern \"held item lock\" fails 1/1 when only the in-lock re-plan is bypassed: stale apply returns ok true and overwrites the competing title. Pattern \"missing session text\" fails 1/1 when only the typed read guard is removed: missing expected CommandError rejection. Each mutation was restored byte-for-byte in finally. Fixed focused run passes 5/5; typecheck, build:test and docstring pass. Initial test setup was corrected to ES2022-compatible barriers and order-insensitive tag assertions; no production contract or gate threshold changed. The five bounded regressions use real non-git trackers, with actual FS reads/locks and no PM SDK mocks."
  "2026-10-22T20:50:22.282Z",codex-agent,"Linked verification passed 4/4 commands: session suite 15/15, typecheck, build:test and docstrings (12 files, 86 declarations). Clarification: the two parser regressions run pure SDK values in bounded child processes; the three stateful regressions use real non-git trackers. Compatibility self-review also retained the old refusal for embedded line separators in a task body, while supporting whitespace separators before the identity. The linked full release commands below use isolated HOME and Git identity at unchanged 97/93/98 floors; no source or dependency scope was excluded."
  "2026-10-22T21:26:20.235Z",codex-agent,"Local full npm gate remains active after more than thirty minutes in real CLI coverage fixtures under shared-host load; no completed local full-gate verdict is claimed. Preserve that run while pushing the focused-tested patch so exact-head CI can execute npm and Bun release:check on Node 22.18.0 and 26 alongside required CodeQL. Focused linked verification already passed 4/4, session suite 15/15, and all five isolated regressions/mutations fail when protection is reverted. Final acceptance will use completed full npm/Bun gate results and the required CodeQL result on the pushed head, distinguishing CI from local evidence. The pinned PM test runner rejected read-only output-budget controls before executing a command; rerunning with JSON output alone started the actual full gate. No dependency or threshold changes."
  "2026-10-22T21:31:41.371Z",codex-agent,"Final timing harness separates SDK imports (60-second startup guard) from parsing (unchanged 2-second assertion plus a 15-second post-import kill watchdog). Explicit ready/done receipts are required, so an early successful child exit cannot pass. A repeated focused run under increased host load exceeded the original startup-inclusive 15-second watchdog; revised parser tests then passed 2/2, and both isolated regex/parser reverts failed 1/1 specifically after imports completed. Other three behavioral revert proofs remain valid and restored. The older local full npm gate was canceled after about 36 minutes because its test harness was superseded; no completed local full gate or local Bun result is claimed. Full npm/Bun acceptance and required CodeQL will be verified from CI on the pushed exact head. Production source protections and coverage floors remain unchanged during this harness adjustment."
  "2026-10-22T21:36:11.910Z",codex-agent,"Required CodeQL result for pushed code head a7f27908d295e50a7e6e5d81f2f18b61dfc1737e is completed/success, verified through the commits check-runs REST endpoint: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-todos/runs/120102728228 . The separate analysis workflow was still completing cleanup at observation time. Both CI runtime jobs passed strict tracked-project health and entered full release checks; npm/Bun acceptance remains pending until those jobs finish. Published PR follow-up content is retained exactly as its prefix, with only an automatic public-safe summary appended by another app; all published text passed the private-path check."
  "2026-10-22T21:46:51.667Z",codex-agent,"Final code-head acceptance for a7f27908d295e50a7e6e5d81f2f18b61dfc1737e: CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-todos/actions/runs/39858200400 completed successfully. Node 22.18.0 and 26 each passed npm run release:check AND bun run release:check. Every one of the four gates reports 321 tests passed, 0 failed/skipped/cancelled/todo; canonical reader 1/1; packed hosts 4/4 (npm-current, bun-current, npm-minimum, bun-minimum). Aggregate L/B/F: 98.03/94.01/98.77 for Node 26 npm/Bun and Node 22 npm; 97.97/93.78/98.77 for Node 22 Bun. Both runtime sources are measured at unchanged 97/93/98 floors. Strict CI tracker health, typechecks, docstrings, build, zero-vulnerability production audit, packaging, changelog/date and publish-attestation checks passed. Required CodeQL check and analysis workflow passed; alert 11 is fixed. The final committed ready/done timing harness was re-proved: reverting only sessionLine or parseTodoTxtLine fails one selected regression after imports, and committed source/test bytes were restored exactly. Other three isolated runtime mutations failed as recorded. Latest complete GraphQL enumeration has zero unresolved threads and no pagination; no new REST review comments appeared after this push. No replies, resolutions, merge or release were performed. Local full execution remains unclaimed after cancellation; completed full acceptance is CI evidence. Release the claim without closing, then commit the public-safe receipt; source and tests remain byte-identical to the accepted code head."
